      "verdict": "partial",
      "gap": "The entry states Definition 2.1 (with the declared extension to inconsistent T), that neither H intersect M = empty nor H union M = V is required, and that hypotheses are atoms. It omits the source's justification and construction for these conventions on p.10: that allowing only positive atoms in solutions is no restriction of generality, because a formula hypothesis F can be represented by adding x <-> F to T for a new variable x added to H; and the reasons for not requiring the two set conditions (a manifestation may explain another; explanations are assumption-based). The handbook instead defers 'general formula hypotheses and their translations' to separate treatments (F 335-338), and no such treatment exists on the route.",
